# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — "React Router: RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action
# Execution Before 400 Response". Affects react-router >=7.12.0 <8.3.0; the
# only fixed version is 8.3.0 (a major upgrade).
# NOT APPLICABLE here: the console frontend is a client-only Vite SPA using
# BrowserRouter/Routes (frontend/src/main.tsx, App.tsx). React Server
# Components / RSC framework mode — the vulnerable surface (server-side
# action execution) — is not used anywhere; the bundle is served as static
# files by FastAPI with no react-router server runtime. Verified 2026-07-25
# (grep: no react-router server imports, no "use server", no @react-router/*
# framework packages). Revisit on any move to react-router v8 or RSC mode.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
